+# Security Policy
+
+## Intended use
+DNS Sinkhole captures and analyses DNS traffic. Run it only on networks and
+hosts you own or are explicitly authorised to monitor.
+
+## Reporting a vulnerability
+Please do **not** open a public issue for security problems. Use GitHub's
+**Security → Report a vulnerability** (private advisory) on this repository,
+or message the maintainer via the LinkedIn link on the GitHub profile.
+
+Include the affected version/commit, reproduction steps and impact. You can
+expect an acknowledgement within 7 days.
+
+## Hardening notes
+- The Flask console has no authentication; bind it to `127.0.0.1` or place it
+  behind an authenticating reverse proxy.
+- Live capture needs elevated privileges; prefer granting `CAP_NET_RAW`
+  to the capture process over running the whole app as root.
+- Uploaded PCAPs are untrusted input; keep the upload size limit enabled.
